1
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:47,600
See? See?

2
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:48,759
What did I tell you?

3
00:00:48,759 --> 00:00:50,399
I said he was definitely lost, but you didn't believe me.

4
00:00:50,399 --> 00:00:51,000
Calm down. Calm down.

5
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,560
This mountain is huge. We need to hurry and search!

6
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,679
Bie Fan!

7
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:54,920
Xiao Li, call for backup.

8
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:55,359
Copy that.

9
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:09,120
Dress left!

10
00:01:23,319 --> 00:01:24,560
Bie Fan

11
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,200
Captain, nothing found in this area.

12
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,439
How did I get down here?

13
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:46,000
We were chased by a tiger.

14
00:03:46,719 --> 00:03:48,560
And accidentally fell down.

15
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,280
I read about this in a book.

16
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:54,520
This is a natural basin.

17
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:55,719
This...

18
00:03:56,439 --> 00:03:57,879
This is a natural graveyard!

19
00:03:59,719 --> 00:04:00,479
Are you okay?

20
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,400
I'm fine. Are you okay?

21
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:06,840
I'm fine. What about the tiger?

22
00:04:07,159 --> 00:04:08,719
The tiger is probably fine too.

23
00:04:12,599 --> 00:04:15,000
Mr. Fang, don't waste your energy.

24
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:16,279
I've already tried.

25
00:04:16,279 --> 00:04:17,480
We can't climb up at all.

26
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,360
What should we do?

27
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:22,279
Don't waste your energy.

28
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:23,879
Let me try.

29
00:04:39,639 --> 00:04:40,439
Try a different one.

30
00:04:40,839 --> 00:04:41,680
This is too high.

31
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,360
There's no signal either.

32
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:48,920
Is anyone there?

33
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,120
Is anyone there?!

34
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,240
Help!

35
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,879
Help!

36
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,839
Is anybody there?!

37
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,399
Is anybody there?!

38
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:03,519
Can you be a little original?

39
00:05:03,519 --> 00:05:05,120
I hate copycats.

40
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:07,639
Fine.

41
00:05:08,319 --> 00:05:09,160
Hello?

42
00:05:10,319 --> 00:05:12,000
Is anyone here?

43
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,800
Tell you what, you keep at it for a bit.

44
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,079
Keep yelling.

45
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,079
Is anyone there?

46
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:28,680
Help us!

47
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,319
We're going to die here!

48
00:05:34,279 --> 00:05:37,199
Come save us!

49
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,199
Help!

50
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:40,120
Stop yelling.

51
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,000
Then it's your turn, Mr. Fang.

52
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,279
No need.

53
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,720
You've been yelling for ages.

54
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:48,000
I'm sure no one's coming.

55
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:55,160
Come drink some water to soothe your throat.

56
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,519
Is it safe to drink?

57
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,279
It's a bit sweet.

58
00:06:11,839 --> 00:06:12,759
Come on, don't be shy. Here.

59
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,240
My stomach hurts.

60
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:20,800
I just held it in, and you brought it right back out.

61
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,439
Mr. Fang!

62
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,680
What do I wipe with?

63
00:06:27,199 --> 00:06:28,399
What did ancient people use?

64
00:06:29,199 --> 00:06:30,000
They used bamboo slips.

65
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,959
Any further back and you've got Cavemen.

66
00:06:34,199 --> 00:06:35,439
They probably used stones.

67
00:06:38,199 --> 00:06:39,160
Here's a stone.

68
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,199
Here.

69
00:06:41,079 --> 00:06:42,399
Mr. Fang.

70
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,120
What are you using?

71
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:44,920
I'm using paper.

72
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,839
I barely have enough for myself.

73
00:06:49,399 --> 00:06:50,360
This paper is super thin.

74
00:06:51,199 --> 00:06:52,160
It tears with a single poke.

75
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:53,240
Manufacturers nowadays...

76
00:06:53,639 --> 00:06:54,040
Look.

77
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,360
My finger went right through.

78
00:07:03,839 --> 00:07:04,839
Mr. Fang.

79
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,079
Are you hungry?

80
00:07:10,199 --> 00:07:11,480
I have food.

81
00:07:12,079 --> 00:07:14,279
Forget it. I'm not eating your crappy berries.

82
00:07:19,839 --> 00:07:20,959
Why do I hear a plastic bag rustling?

83
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:22,639
What?

84
00:07:23,879 --> 00:07:24,480
What's that?

85
00:07:25,519 --> 00:07:26,360
What the hell is that?

86
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,279
Buns? What... Are those buns?

87
00:07:29,279 --> 00:07:30,040
Are they?

88
00:07:31,879 --> 00:07:32,439
Yeah.

89
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:33,360
Where did you get buns?

90
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,519
Rong Sihai gave them to me.

91
00:07:35,519 --> 00:07:36,279
When we were eating berries yesterday...

92
00:07:36,279 --> 00:07:37,160
Why didn't you take them out?

93
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:40,920
I forgot.

94
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,600
What else is in your bag?

95
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,480
In that bag!

96
00:07:47,839 --> 00:07:48,680
This book.

97
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,839
I picked it back up.

98
00:07:56,839 --> 00:07:58,600
Why is there hotpot base in here?

99
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:02,480
It's a local specialty. I wanted to bring some for Rong Sihai.

100
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,439
What else do you have to eat?

101
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:05,399
I also have chicken feet.

102
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,319
You really kept something up your sleeve, huh.

103
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,319
Got any more food?

104
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,120
Hold on a second.

105
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,639
For a dying man,

106
00:08:29,639 --> 00:08:31,120
food really isn't that important.

107
00:08:31,879 --> 00:08:32,759
Stop eating for a second.

108
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:35,519
But it's different for you.

109
00:08:35,919 --> 00:08:36,879
You have to make it out of here.

110
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:38,200
So I think this...

111
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,159
one and a half Youtiao...

112
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,440
we need to ration it.

113
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:45,399
More accurately, you need to ration it.

114
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:49,799
Here.

115
00:08:49,919 --> 00:08:50,639
Since we...

116
00:08:50,639 --> 00:08:52,399
don't know when rescue will come,

117
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:53,559
we need to divide this Youtiao...

118
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:54,320
into seven portions.

119
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,080
That way, you can last seven days.

120
00:09:01,559 --> 00:09:02,440
Mr. Fang.

121
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:05,200
If you're giving me all seven portions of the Youtiao,

122
00:09:05,759 --> 00:09:06,639
what about you?

123
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,840
A person can survive at most seven days without food.

124
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:12,559
And after seven days, when the Youtiao is gone,

125
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:13,960
what do I eat then?

126
00:09:20,279 --> 00:09:21,320
You can just eat me.

127
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:25,759
Stop talking.

128
00:09:26,519 --> 00:09:27,799
Getting emotional wastes energy too. Come on.

129
00:09:29,039 --> 00:09:29,960
Let's just lie down and sleep.

130
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,799
One, two, three, four

131
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:09,840
Five, six

132
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,000
Six, seven

133
00:10:30,679 --> 00:10:31,279
Smells so good.

134
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:36,799
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven.

135
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,559
No change.

136
00:10:39,559 --> 00:10:40,440
Looks like they didn't eat at all.

137
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,320
Can't tell.

138
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,519
This one looks a bit big.

139
00:10:52,279 --> 00:10:54,840
But they'd all look big if they ate it.

140
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:55,559
Right.

141
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,360
How are we supposed to tell?

142
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,240
I can't even tell them apart.

143
00:11:03,679 --> 00:11:04,480
Doesn't make a difference.

144
00:11:08,519 --> 00:11:10,159
True. This one is way too big.

145
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,159
Screw you all!

146
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,440
You tiny little things!

147
00:11:26,399 --> 00:11:27,440
Where is your conscience?

148
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:29,159
What I can't figure out is...

149
00:11:29,159 --> 00:11:30,960
How such a tiny rat like you...

150
00:11:31,159 --> 00:11:33,279
could eat a whole one and a half Youtiao!

151
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,639
Do you really think

152
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:36,159
what you ate was... was Youtiao?

153
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,559
You ate Bie Fan's

154
00:11:39,799 --> 00:11:41,399
last shred of hope!

155
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,559
Mr. Fang.

156
00:11:44,919 --> 00:11:46,480
Stop yelling.

157
00:11:46,919 --> 00:11:49,240
You haven't eaten for a long time either.

158
00:11:49,279 --> 00:11:51,279
Save some energy.

159
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:54,720
I should've let you eat some yesterday.

160
00:11:57,279 --> 00:12:00,200
Damn rat! Stealing our stuff...

161
00:12:00,799 --> 00:12:02,080
You'll die a horrible death!

162
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:04,480
Your whole family will die a horrible death!

163
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:04,960
Bie Fan.

164
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,600
Just wait till I get out! I'll get rat poison...

165
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,799
Bie Fan! I'll kill you all...

166
00:12:07,799 --> 00:12:09,200
Fanfan! Fanfan! Fanfan!

167
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,360
Al... Alright, that's enough.

168
00:12:11,159 --> 00:12:12,600
That rat isn't from Shandong, it doesn't understand.

169
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,519
It's from a cave.

170
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,080
Cursing at it won't get you an answer.

171
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,960
It's just a rat, after all.

172
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:19,120
Alright, calm down.

173
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,279
I'm so cold and hungry.

174
00:12:25,519 --> 00:12:28,279
I feel like I'm about to be...

175
00:12:29,279 --> 00:12:30,320
about to die.

176
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,679
Can you not touch my backpack, Mr. Fang?

177
00:12:58,519 --> 00:12:59,799
Mr. Fang.

178
00:13:01,759 --> 00:13:04,279
Thank you. You're really nice.

179
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:08,919
No one's ever hugged me before.

180
00:13:09,399 --> 00:13:11,879
Only my mom has hugged me.

181
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,320
What if you turn around? Would it be

182
00:13:15,679 --> 00:13:16,799
a little warmer?

183
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:29,879
How about I turn around and you hold me.

184
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:37,279
About you holding me while we sleep...

185
00:13:39,879 --> 00:13:40,519
once you get out of here,

186
00:13:40,519 --> 00:13:41,799
don't tell anyone about it.

187
00:13:42,799 --> 00:13:44,120
This could easily go viral.

188
00:13:46,919 --> 00:13:48,120
Mr. Fang,

189
00:13:48,919 --> 00:13:53,440
do you think we can still get out?

190
00:13:53,759 --> 00:13:56,559
Are we going to die here?

191
00:13:57,679 --> 00:13:58,679
Dying here isn't so bad.

192
00:13:59,799 --> 00:14:00,720
Suits me fine.

193
00:14:02,039 --> 00:14:04,320
Are we really going to die here?

194
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:07,360
What about the restaurant then?

195
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:11,159
What about Rong Sihai? What do we do?

196
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:14,799
My mom's ashes are still in the restaurant!

197
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:16,519
Wow, the hometown dialect just slipped out.

198
00:14:19,039 --> 00:14:21,039
Why are you yelling? I'm just kidding.

199
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,240
I don't want to die.

200
00:14:23,519 --> 00:14:24,639
I was just joking!

201
00:14:26,879 --> 00:14:28,480
It's not funny at all.

202
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:31,919
Mr. Fang,

203
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:34,360
I don't want to die.

204
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,960
And I don't want you to die either.

205
00:14:37,759 --> 00:14:39,559
I've never been able to figure out...

206
00:14:39,639 --> 00:14:41,840
why do you want to die?

207
00:14:44,519 --> 00:14:46,360
I can't find any meaning in living.

208
00:14:46,679 --> 00:14:49,320
Does living have to have a meaning?

209
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,720
Of course it has to have a meaning.

210
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,960
I don't know what

211
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,639
the meaning of my life is either,

212
00:14:55,879 --> 00:14:58,919
but I'm just happy to be alive!

213
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,519
But for someone like you,

214
00:15:02,639 --> 00:15:03,919
you have a small restaurant,

215
00:15:04,759 --> 00:15:05,759
a small business,

216
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,159
you have Rong Sihai,

217
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,480
you have friends,

218
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,279
and your mom's ashes to keep you company,

219
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:16,799
Bie Fan.

220
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:18,960
What about me?

221
00:15:22,279 --> 00:15:23,360
I have nothing.

222
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,600
I have absolutely nothing on this earth.

223
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:37,919
No one loves me.

224
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:41,919
I have no friends.

225
00:15:44,879 --> 00:15:45,919
No family.

226
00:15:52,279 --> 00:15:53,039
No house.

227
00:15:54,039 --> 00:15:54,879
No car.

228
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,200
No money.

229
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,399
I've written books on success,

230
00:16:01,399 --> 00:16:03,000
but I'm not successful myself.

231
00:16:04,759 --> 00:16:05,960
I'm 41 this year.

232
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,759
My hair's turned white.

233
00:16:09,799 --> 00:16:11,360
I've worked hard for half my life,

234
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,399
and ended up with nothing... absolutely nothing.

235
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,559
I take the subway alone,

236
00:16:16,919 --> 00:16:18,039
watch movies alone,

237
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,720
eat alone,

238
00:16:20,399 --> 00:16:21,559
go to the doctor alone.

239
00:16:21,879 --> 00:16:25,159
I'm just living alone, struggling all by myself.

240
00:16:28,559 --> 00:16:30,080
No one has ever acknowledged me.

241
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,879
Now I don't even have my dignity left.

242
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:42,200
Tell me, what is the meaning of my life?

243
00:16:51,399 --> 00:16:52,240
Then...

244
00:16:54,919 --> 00:16:58,919
then I'll be your friend from now on.

245
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,320
Okay?

246
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,559
Mr. Fang, what... what are you doing?

247
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,000
Fan, Mr. Fang has an announcement to make.

248
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,839
No matter what,

249
00:17:36,279 --> 00:17:38,039
I'm going to get you out of here alive.

250
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:42,880
You scared me to death.

251
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,799
I thought you were going to kill yourself again.

252
00:17:45,599 --> 00:17:46,920
Su... Suicide? What suicide?

253
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,519
Can we get up there?

254
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,839
Let's give it a try.

255
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,400
As long as our minds don't slip,

256
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,519
there are always more solutions than problems.

257
00:17:53,079 --> 00:17:54,319
If you're really starving,

258
00:17:54,319 --> 00:17:56,519
why don't you eat some hotpot base?

259
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,160
Wait, you...

260
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:12,400
totally baffled me.

261
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:15,160
Who just eats it raw like that!

262
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:16,079
Spicy!

263
00:18:18,359 --> 00:18:19,079
Oh my God!

264
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,359
Bie Fan! Bie Fan!

265
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,960
What? You're... you're still drinking that water?

266
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:23,960
I'm out of toilet paper!

267
00:18:24,519 --> 00:18:25,839
It's spicy!

268
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,519
No, let's boil it.

269
00:18:27,519 --> 00:18:29,160
Wait, wait, boil it before drinking!

270
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:30,839
We don't have fire.

271
00:18:31,319 --> 00:18:33,440
No fire? We just need to make a fire, then.

272
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:34,920
We'll figure out a way to start a fire.

273
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,079
Isn't that super simple?

274
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,839
In ancient times, there was a sage.

275
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:39,599
From a bird pecking at a suimu tree,

276
00:18:39,599 --> 00:18:40,480
he found inspiration.

277
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:43,039
So, he broke off some suimu branches,

278
00:18:43,039 --> 00:18:44,000
and made fire by friction.

279
00:18:44,079 --> 00:18:47,200
Later, people revered him as Suiren Shi,

280
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,279
and honored him as the head of the Three Sovereigns.

281
00:18:49,279 --> 00:18:50,599
In the past, Bo Yi dug wells,

282
00:18:50,599 --> 00:18:51,680
and Suiren made fire by friction.

283
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,880
The power of water and fire

284
00:18:53,359 --> 00:18:56,759
is still relied upon today.

285
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,680
The stick is too wet.

286
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,519
This stick...

287
00:19:00,039 --> 00:19:01,480
It's really damp out here.

288
00:19:03,599 --> 00:19:04,720
Mr. Fang...

289
00:19:05,119 --> 00:19:07,599
Why don't you use a lighter?

290
00:19:08,839 --> 00:19:10,480
You have a lighter and didn't say so earlier?

291
00:19:12,599 --> 00:19:14,160
I don't have a lighter.

292
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:15,599
I guessed as much.

293
00:19:18,079 --> 00:19:19,640
Then why did you ask that question?

294
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,880
Right, why did I ask that question?

295
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:24,519
Get lost.

296
00:19:35,519 --> 00:19:36,200
Bie Fan

297
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:41,240
A concave-convex lens is a type of curved mirror.

298
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:44,559
One side is convex, the other concave.

299
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:47,000
When light passes through it,

300
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,640
and focuses on this focal point,

301
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,039
the area right at this point,

302
00:19:49,039 --> 00:19:50,799
its temperature will rise accordingly.

303
00:19:55,039 --> 00:19:57,720
This surface isn't convex enough. The main issue is...

304
00:20:07,079 --> 00:20:10,599
It's lit! It's lit! It's lit!

305
00:20:15,759 --> 00:20:18,119
It's lit! It's lit!

306
00:20:18,359 --> 00:20:20,720
Water has a relatively high heat-absorbing capacity.

307
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:22,440
A very strong capacity.

308
00:20:22,599 --> 00:20:24,880
So, when this flame

309
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,759
touches the plastic bag filled with water,

310
00:20:26,759 --> 00:20:28,559
the water will rapidly absorb the heat,

311
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,079
until it boils.

312
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,079
So we have...

313
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:36,160
It went out.

314
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,359
Fill it with water. Light it again for me.

315
00:20:45,319 --> 00:20:46,680
Therefore, science must

316
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:47,960
undergo countless experiments

317
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,200
to reach the ultimate truth.

318
00:20:51,799 --> 00:20:55,000
That's the cup Rong Sihai gave me.

319
00:20:58,039 --> 00:20:59,279
Say thanks to Rong Sihai for me.

320
00:21:02,359 --> 00:21:03,799
Our water problem is solved now.

321
00:21:03,799 --> 00:21:04,960
Let's start looking for food.

322
00:21:05,119 --> 00:21:05,720
Come on.

323
00:21:08,759 --> 00:21:10,480
There must be a big catch under the tree!

324
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,079
Look, ants.

325
00:21:14,279 --> 00:21:15,440
Ants are high in protein.

326
00:21:15,759 --> 00:21:17,279
Look, the ants are moving.

327
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,920
Should we eat their whole family?

328
00:21:19,559 --> 00:21:21,559
Is this stuff even edible?

329
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,079
You try it.

330
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,119
Let's call it the whole colony.

331
00:21:24,119 --> 00:21:25,160
Come on, all of you.

332
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,519
Don't rush now, come on.

333
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,680
This isn't filling at all.

334
00:21:31,599 --> 00:21:32,720
Not much meat, huh?

335
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,240
Bie Fan, come here!

336
00:21:39,039 --> 00:21:39,880
Come here, Bie Fan.

337
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:42,200
There's no spider here.

338
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,359
This web here...

339
00:21:44,359 --> 00:21:45,359
is actually a trap.

340
00:21:45,599 --> 00:21:47,359
It has to wait until some food gets stuck on it,

341
00:21:47,359 --> 00:21:48,000
and then the spider will come out.

342
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,200
Just stand right next to it. Stand there

343
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:50,799
and pretend to be prey for once.

344
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:53,880
Don't move!

345
00:21:54,759 --> 00:21:56,960
Here's a toad.

346
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:59,000
Earthworms, spiders,

347
00:21:59,279 --> 00:22:00,279
snails,

348
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:02,119
and a whole family of geckos.

349
00:22:03,559 --> 00:22:04,480
How should we cook them?

350
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,519
Clear broth, simmer over low heat.

351
00:22:15,119 --> 00:22:16,160
You're younger, you pick first.

352
00:22:17,279 --> 00:22:19,640
Then I'll just pick one.

353
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:20,960
You can have the rest.

354
00:22:21,759 --> 00:22:22,799
No worries, come on.

355
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,559
I let you pick.

356
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:37,039
You sure know how to pick.

357
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,119
You take the big one.

358
00:22:38,119 --> 00:22:39,559
Then what about the other three?

359
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:40,400
I'll eat the big one.

360
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,400
The rest... the rest are all yours.

361
00:22:42,559 --> 00:22:45,160
Bro, I'm too scared to eat that spider.

362
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,160
A spider? You think I'd dare eat it?

363
00:22:48,799 --> 00:22:50,279
Shut up. We're splitting it in half.

364
00:22:51,079 --> 00:22:51,880
You have to eat it.

365
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:53,400
This half is yours.

366
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,039
This half is mine.

367
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:54,640
And there's this snail.

368
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,200
You can have the big one.

369
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,240
Here, the spider.

370
00:22:56,839 --> 00:22:58,880
I'm too scared, bro.

371
00:23:01,799 --> 00:23:02,960
What are you afraid of? It's fine.

372
00:23:03,119 --> 00:23:03,880
You... you...

373
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,759
Just pretend it's like...

374
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,799
You pretend it's... Even poop looks better than this!

375
00:23:09,079 --> 00:23:10,480
Just... just close your eyes and eat it.

376
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,440
Not bad. Not bad at all.

377
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:24,799
Oh, my god.

378
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:25,559
Pretty good. This is pretty good.

379
00:23:25,559 --> 00:23:26,559
It's tolerable.

380
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,839
Come on, you have some too. Quick, come here.

381
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,680
Bro, I'm too scared to eat it.

382
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:32,960
Get over here and eat. I already finished mine.

383
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,680
Hurry up. Get over here.

384
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:36,400
Open your mouth.

385
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:48,440
Hold it in.

386
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:49,480
Throwing up will just make you hungrier.

387
00:23:53,119 --> 00:23:56,160
I kind of regret this, Mr. Fang.

388
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,400
I'm telling you, I hate people like you.

389
00:23:57,400 --> 00:23:58,720
Who knows that the food on the plate...

390
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:00,599
Every root...

391
00:24:01,279 --> 00:24:02,039
Every bug...

392
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,200
Every worm...

393
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,000
Every lump comes from hard work.

394
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:12,160
Mr. Fang, is that long thing a bug?

395
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,079
What long thing?

396
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,400
What bug? That's poop.

397
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:19,039
Did you poop that out?

398
00:24:19,039 --> 00:24:19,960
What would I even poop out?

399
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:20,599
Have I eaten anything?

400
00:24:20,599 --> 00:24:21,880
How could I poop that much?

401
00:24:22,079 --> 00:24:24,319
Well, I didn't poop it out either.

402
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,400
Why is it so big?

403
00:24:34,119 --> 00:24:35,599
Why is the poop standing up?

404
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:39,160
Have we run into a Poop Monster?

405
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:40,759
A Poop Monster?

406
00:24:41,079 --> 00:24:42,240
Poop can turn into a monster?

407
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:48,079
Run! Get up, get up, get up!

408
00:24:51,119 --> 00:24:53,519
Mr. Fang! Mr. Fang!

409
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:56,400
Don't panic!

410
00:24:57,359 --> 00:24:58,960
Go... go... go to hell!

411
00:25:00,039 --> 00:25:01,680
Go, go, go!

412
00:25:07,319 --> 00:25:10,400
Mr. Fang, is it going to eat us?

413
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:11,559
Look, look! Didn't you see?

414
00:25:11,559 --> 00:25:12,799
This... this snake is afraid of fire.

415
00:25:12,799 --> 00:25:14,079
As long as we have this fire,

416
00:25:14,279 --> 00:25:15,160
it won't dare come near.

417
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:17,839
What if you get tired of holding it?

418
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:19,240
We'll take turns.

419
00:25:19,640 --> 00:25:20,279
We'll outlast it.

420
00:25:28,599 --> 00:25:29,400
Where did you come from?

421
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:31,839
Go back to whatever you were doing!

422
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:36,960
We are pests!

423
00:25:36,960 --> 00:25:38,279
Ready, sing!

424
00:25:40,119 --> 00:25:40,759
Sing!

425
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:00,400
Where's the snake?

426
00:26:09,319 --> 00:26:10,160
Stay back!

427
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:11,720
Here, Mr. Fang.

428
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:15,240
Mr. Fang.

429
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:17,599
I'm hungry and sleepy right now.

430
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:20,880
Do you think it'll eat us?

431
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:23,920
Either it eats us

432
00:26:25,519 --> 00:26:26,839
and turns us into poop,

433
00:26:27,119 --> 00:26:29,039
or we eat this Poop Monster

434
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:31,000
and turn it into poop.

435
00:26:59,359 --> 00:27:00,880
You'd better get to a hospital.

436
00:27:02,279 --> 00:27:04,960
We can't get out.
